<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Britannia Superior</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Britannia Superior was the southern of the two provinces into which Roman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> was divided in the early third century, governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/londinium">Londinium</a> (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>) and including the legions at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caerleon">Caerleon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chester">Chester</a>. The division, attributed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a> or <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caracalla">Caracalla</a>, aimed to stop any single governor controlling all three British legions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/britannia-superior.jpg" alt="Britannia Superior" width="320" height="267" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tomisti · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roman_Empire_-_Britannia_Superior_(AD_210).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
